Terraform Provisioners & Modules

Today I explored two powerful features of Terraform: Provisioners and Modules.

🔹 Provisioners

Used when we need to run scripts or commands inside a resource after it is created.

Example: installing software on a new VM.

Types:

remote-exec → runs commands on the target machine.

local-exec → runs commands on your local machine.


💡 Best practice: use provisioners only when necessary; configuration tools (like Ansible) are usually better.


🔹 Modules

A module is just a collection of Terraform files reused across projects.

Think of them as functions in programming – you write once, use many times.

Benefits:

Reusability

Clean and organized code

Easier collaboration in teams
